hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16747","Abd Allah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayda, meaning al-Haddad, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Mansur, from Dhu al-Lihya al-Kilabi, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act in a new matter or in a matter already finished; he said: No, rather in a matter already finished; he said: Then for what do we act; he said: Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for."
"16748","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Abd Allah al-Basri narrated to us, Sahl ibn Aslam al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Mansur narrated to us, from Dhu al-Lihya al-Kilabi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do we act in a new matter or in a matter already finished; he said: Rather in a matter already finished; he said: Then for what is action; he said: Act, for each is facilitated for what he was created for."
